00:00:17.280 --> 00:00:18.480
Welcome to Horror History.

00:00:18.480 --> 00:00:20.020
"Who'd want a history of this toilet?"

00:00:20.220 --> 00:00:24.900
My name is Abraham Lincoln: Taco Hunter and
this time I’m not the only Horror Hist…

00:00:24.910 --> 00:00:28.020
orian of the episode because I’m covering
Mike Hanlon.

00:00:28.020 --> 00:00:31.800
Mike was the seventh and final piece of the
Losers Club -- a researcher who used his knowledge

00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:35.600
to help guide his friends in the right direction
to be able to understand and take down their

00:00:35.600 --> 00:00:36.760
supernatural rival.

00:00:36.760 --> 00:00:40.089
To understand why Mike became interested in
cataloguing the history of Derry, we’ll

00:00:40.089 --> 00:00:45.440
have to dig into some history texts as well,
starting with Mike’s earliest days of infancy.

00:00:45.440 --> 00:00:47.960
[HORROR HISTORY]

00:00:47.960 --> 00:00:53.319
Michael Hanlon became the only child of William
and Jessica Hanlon in 1946 and was born into

00:00:53.319 --> 00:00:54.510
a life of farming.

00:00:54.510 --> 00:00:58.620
One day, when Mike was only a baby, the weather
outside was nice, so Jessica took her sons

00:00:58.620 --> 00:01:03.640
crib outside so they could enjoy some sunshine,
where baby Mike was attacked by a wild bird,

00:01:03.640 --> 00:01:05.930
which pecked at him until his mother shooed
it away.

00:01:05.930 --> 00:01:09.670
This trauma somehow stuck with Mike into his
older years, where he would continue to have

00:01:09.670 --> 00:01:10.670
a fear of birds.

00:01:10.670 --> 00:01:14.860
He grew up helping his father man the farm,
which he was paid for, and received a 5% stake

00:01:14.860 --> 00:01:17.939
in the business in order for Will to teach
him the value of hard work.

00:01:17.939 --> 00:01:22.450
The work consisted of picking peas, radishes,
beans, potatoes, pumpkins and squash.

00:01:22.450 --> 00:01:26.789
In 1951, Mike began school at the Neibolt
Church Street School, a religious institution

00:01:26.789 --> 00:01:30.520
that kept him from meeting many of the kids
his age in town who attended Derry Elementary,

00:01:30.520 --> 00:01:34.100
leaving him to fill the time his father gave
him off of work in the summers by himself.

00:01:34.100 --> 00:01:38.119
The Hanlons sometimes had trouble with their
racist neighbor, Butch Bowers, and not long

00:01:38.119 --> 00:01:42.670
before the Spring of 1958, Butch’s son Henry
joined in on the torment when he killed the

00:01:42.670 --> 00:01:45.009
Hanlons’ dog Mr. Chips by feeding him a
poisoned burger.

00:01:45.009 --> 00:01:49.039
It was at this point when Will felt it necessary
to teach his son about some of the evil people

00:01:49.039 --> 00:01:53.100
that inhabit Derry, explaining that Butch
was crazy and that he should stay away from

00:01:53.100 --> 00:01:54.100
Henry.

00:01:54.100 --> 00:01:57.770
He goes onto explain some of the inexplicable
acts of racism throughout Derry’s history.

00:01:57.770 --> 00:02:01.840
Will was somewhat of an amateur historian
himself, and kept a photo album that documented

00:02:01.840 --> 00:02:03.280
certain events from Derry’s past.

00:02:03.280 --> 00:02:07.241
He used this to teach his son how stay on
guard, and I think sparked Mike’s interest

00:02:07.241 --> 00:02:08.730
in studying the past.

00:02:08.730 --> 00:02:12.000
Mike also learned how to drive the tractor
from his father and each year they would do

00:02:12.000 --> 00:02:13.000
a rock harvest.

00:02:13.000 --> 00:02:16.140
Although Mike enjoyed playing in the snow
during the winter, he always felt a sadness

00:02:16.140 --> 00:02:18.170
when the harvest season came to an end.

00:02:18.170 --> 00:02:21.860
Will instilled a strong sense of morality
into his son by giving him small tasks to

00:02:21.860 --> 00:02:25.251
teach him life lessons, or take him on day
trips, like when he took his son to the police

00:02:25.251 --> 00:02:29.090
station to see the Tramp Chair, a restraining
device used earlier in the century to punish

00:02:29.090 --> 00:02:30.090
wrongdoers.

00:02:30.090 --> 00:02:33.200
One day, Mike discovers a note from his father
telling him to go check out the remains of

00:02:33.200 --> 00:02:37.830
the old Ironworks that exploded in 1906, an
activity meant to clue Mike in on violent

00:02:37.830 --> 00:02:39.330
patterns of Derry’s past.

00:02:39.330 --> 00:02:42.750
This was only one day after he had watched
the movie Rodan with his dad, and when he

00:02:42.750 --> 00:02:46.430
arrived at the ruins, he discovered a giant
bird hiding in the cellar hole.

00:02:46.430 --> 00:02:50.260
Mike ran, and the bird swooped in to try to
pick him up, so he took refuge in the smoke

00:02:50.260 --> 00:02:51.260
stack.

00:02:51.260 --> 00:02:54.040
The bird tried to squeeze into the enclosure
with him, and Mike was only able to drive

00:02:54.040 --> 00:02:58.750
it away by throwing pieces of tile, and getting
some assistance from some unknown force helping

00:02:58.750 --> 00:03:01.250
him throw harder, likely It’s rival the
Turtle.

00:03:01.250 --> 00:03:04.700
One of the pieces of tile pierces the bird
and it disappears.

00:03:04.700 --> 00:03:08.430
When Mike gets home, his father regrets telling
him to go over there without Mike even having

00:03:08.430 --> 00:03:09.680
shared what had happened.

00:03:09.680 --> 00:03:14.640
I think Will is somewhat privy to the effects
of It that haunt Derry and senses the Ironworks

00:03:14.640 --> 00:03:18.470
could be dangerous, even if he wasn't aware of the monster itself in the same way

00:03:18.470 --> 00:03:19.470
Mike is.

00:03:19.470 --> 00:03:22.990
A couple months later in June, on the first
day of summer vacation, Mike went over to

00:03:22.990 --> 00:03:27.180
Bassey Park near the canal and smelled a salty
old sea smell in the morning fog that gave

00:03:27.180 --> 00:03:28.480
him a sense of danger.

00:03:28.480 --> 00:03:32.140
He discovered a pocket knife with the initials
E.C. in the grass, and was going to take it

00:03:32.140 --> 00:03:34.370
for himself until he saw blood.

00:03:34.370 --> 00:03:37.540
This makes him think of the bird from the
Ironworks, but he pushes the thought away.

00:03:37.540 --> 00:03:41.380
He follows a set of grooves in the grass,
and they lead him to a bloody piece of cloth

00:03:41.380 --> 00:03:43.340
and dried blood at the canal’s edge.

00:03:43.340 --> 00:03:47.540
He sees something move in the outflow tunnel,
then hears a loud splash that causes him to

00:03:47.540 --> 00:03:51.430
throw the knife into the canal and run to
his bike, but he could hear wet footsteps

00:03:51.430 --> 00:03:53.300
following him in the grass.

00:03:53.300 --> 00:03:57.430
He would later hear of the disappearance of
a boy named Edward Corcoran, most likely connected

00:03:57.430 --> 00:03:59.680
to the blade he found with the letters E.C.

00:03:59.680 --> 00:04:02.980
Mike was the biggest target of the town’s
most prominent bully Henry Bowers.

00:04:02.980 --> 00:04:07.571
Well I guess Ben was technically the biggest
target, but Mike was Henry’s favorite target

00:04:07.571 --> 00:04:09.910
because of the rivalry between their fathers.

00:04:09.910 --> 00:04:14.030
In July of 1958, Henry and his gang were targeting
Mike on a regular basis.

00:04:14.030 --> 00:04:17.850
On July 3rd, they chased after him while he
was on his way to a marching band rehearsal.

00:04:17.850 --> 00:04:21.250
Mike played the trombone, and this would be
the last rehearsal before their Independence

00:04:21.250 --> 00:04:22.250
Day performance.

00:04:22.250 --> 00:04:26.090
The bullies chase him down to the abandoned
property at 29 Neibolt Street and Henry reveals

00:04:26.090 --> 00:04:30.570
that he was the one that killed Mike’s dog,
causing Mike to snap and throw at rock at

00:04:30.570 --> 00:04:32.270
Henry’s forehead, causing it to bleed.

00:04:32.270 --> 00:04:36.060
He climbs over the fence to escape, but Henry
catches his shoe as he does, so Mike kicks

00:04:36.060 --> 00:04:37.620
down and breaks Henry’s nose.

00:04:37.620 --> 00:04:41.620
The chase continues to the gravel pit in the
Barrens, where Mike fortunately runs into

00:04:41.620 --> 00:04:46.280
Bill Denbrough, Ben Hanscom, Beverly Marsh,
Eddie Kaspbrak, Richie Tozier and Stan Uris.

00:04:46.280 --> 00:04:49.940
An epic rock fight ensues, and the kids are
able to drive away Henry’s gang.

00:04:49.940 --> 00:04:54.580
“I think the six of us can put you in the
hospital.”

00:04:54.580 --> 00:04:55.580
“Seven.”

00:04:55.580 --> 00:04:59.890
That was the moment that Mike Hanlon joined
the Losers Club, a name given to them by Henry

00:04:59.890 --> 00:05:01.000
Bowers himself.

00:05:01.000 --> 00:05:04.950
Mike could relate to these kids, because just
like he is bullied by Henry for his skin color,

00:05:04.950 --> 00:05:08.110
each of them have something about them that
caused Henry and his gang to go after them.

00:05:08.110 --> 00:05:13.080
Bill had his stutter, Eddie his asthma, Ben
his weight, Beverly her scandalous reputation,

00:05:13.080 --> 00:05:15.350
Richie his glasses, and Stan his Torah.

00:05:15.350 --> 00:05:18.430
The group got to know Mike, but they would
not bring up their encounters with Pennywise

00:05:18.430 --> 00:05:22.080
just yet, and although the movies don’t
cover it, the next day Mike would have his

00:05:22.080 --> 00:05:25.380
first encounter with It in its favorite form.

00:05:28.710 --> 00:05:31.740
One of Mike Hanlon’s greatest strengths
was his ability to document everything that

00:05:31.740 --> 00:05:33.400
occurred in Derry to use against Pennywise.

00:05:33.400 --> 00:05:37.370
