00:06:50.080 --> 00:06:51.680
Ahh, July 4th.

00:06:51.699 --> 00:06:52.889
American Independence Day.

00:06:52.889 --> 00:06:58.840
A day for barbeques, fireworks, parades and
an ancient evil creature that feeds off of

00:06:58.840 --> 00:07:00.840
childrens’ fears -- OK who created this
holiday?

00:07:00.840 --> 00:07:04.400
As Mike was marching for the Neibolt Church
Street School band’s annual parade, he noticed

00:07:04.400 --> 00:07:08.060
a clown handing out balloons to children on
the side of the road and got a feeling from

00:07:08.060 --> 00:07:10.420
the clown that reminded him of the giant bird.

00:07:10.420 --> 00:07:14.389
The clown made eye contact and waved at Mike,
as if it had read his mind.

00:07:14.389 --> 00:07:18.480
Mike’s trombone went silent as his mouth
dried up at this sight; somehow seeing the

00:07:18.480 --> 00:07:21.440
clown felt even worse than seeing Henry Bowers.

00:07:21.440 --> 00:07:25.500
Later on up the hill, he came across the clown
again, and wondered how it was possible for

00:07:25.500 --> 00:07:27.800
It to have gotten past the marching band that
quickly.

00:07:27.800 --> 00:07:32.400
This time, many of the children were crying,
and once again, Pennywise waved to Mike.

00:07:32.400 --> 00:07:36.431
This is when he recognized the creature from
Derry’s deep past in his father’s photo

00:07:36.440 --> 00:07:37.431
album.

00:07:37.440 --> 00:07:40.680
He would share the discovery with his friends
two days later, and the kids would plan

00:07:40.680 --> 00:07:42.889
how they could kill It for the first time.

00:07:42.889 --> 00:07:46.440
They also start construction on a clubhouse
in the Barrens and the following week, Mike

00:07:46.440 --> 00:07:49.320
would bring the photo album along to share
what he knew with the others.

00:07:49.320 --> 00:07:52.979
This is basically Mike taking the role of
chief historian of the Losers Club, perhaps

00:07:52.979 --> 00:07:56.740
the most important part any of them would
take on as Mike would soon find out.

00:07:56.740 --> 00:08:02.580
He shows them Pennywise cameos in pictures
dating back to the early 1700s, then a 1945

00:08:02.580 --> 00:08:06.610
photo comes to life and Pennywise terrorizes
them by morphing into it’s many scary forms

00:08:06.610 --> 00:08:09.280
like the werewolf, leper, mummy and dead boys.

00:08:09.280 --> 00:08:13.220
In late July, the Losers Club decides to try
conducting a smoke hole ceremony, an Indian

00:08:13.220 --> 00:08:17.120
ritual used to help tribesmen make big decisions
by breathing in a lot of smoke and having

00:08:17.120 --> 00:08:19.190
hallucinations of the best path forward.

00:08:19.190 --> 00:08:22.980
Do not try this at home, you’ll just die
or get cancer.

00:08:22.980 --> 00:08:26.460
They start a bonfire in the clubhouse and
one-by-one, they jump out when it becomes

00:08:26.460 --> 00:08:28.720
too hard to breathe, leaving only Richie and
Mike.

00:08:28.720 --> 00:08:32.809
They see the inside of the tiny clubhouse
start to expand, leaving them in a huge space

00:08:32.809 --> 00:08:34.349
the size of a ballroom.

00:08:34.349 --> 00:08:37.979
Smoke clouds their vision, then they feel
themselves start to float up until Mike realizes

00:08:37.979 --> 00:08:41.589
that they are no longer inside of the confines
of the clubhouse, but rather outside in the

00:08:41.589 --> 00:08:45.079
Barrens, although these were not the Barrens
as Richie and Mike knew them.

00:08:45.079 --> 00:08:49.430
These were the Barrens as they looked millions
of years ago: no standpipe, no houses, but

00:08:49.430 --> 00:08:52.990
lots more animal wildlife such as bats, jumping
fish and antelope.

00:08:52.990 --> 00:08:56.269
The animals flee the area and they feel as
if they know what’s about to happen, they

00:08:56.269 --> 00:08:58.830
can feel the presence of It drawing ever closer.

00:08:58.830 --> 00:09:02.230
A burning object pieces through the clouds,
and Mike and Richie run for it.

00:09:02.230 --> 00:09:04.921
The next thing they know, they’re being
pulled out of the clubhouse and out of the

00:09:04.921 --> 00:09:06.639
hallucination by the others.

00:09:06.639 --> 00:09:10.279
Richie passes out, but upon coming back to,
he and Mike tell the story about how they

00:09:10.279 --> 00:09:13.720
were able to view the arrival of It, crash
landing from outer-space.

00:09:13.720 --> 00:09:18.040
I find it most fitting that it was the group’s
seer and the historian who were there to witness

00:09:18.040 --> 00:09:20.940
and pass on the story of this historical event.

00:09:20.940 --> 00:09:23.490
The plotting against It continues, throughout
the month.

00:09:23.490 --> 00:09:27.139
Mike joins the others in visiting Eddie Kaspbrak
in the hospital after his arm is broken, and

00:09:27.139 --> 00:09:31.839
Mike again experiences the dirty prejudices
that corrupt many citizens of Derry when Eddie’s

00:09:31.839 --> 00:09:35.449
mom gives him an especially disdainful look
while telling off the six of them.

00:09:35.449 --> 00:09:38.790
They go to the Barrens to take turns practicing
with the slingshot to determine who should

00:09:38.790 --> 00:09:40.800
be the one to wield it against the monster.

00:09:40.800 --> 00:09:45.180
Mike holds the best record by hitting a respectable
5 out of 10 cans until Beverly came and slam

00:09:45.180 --> 00:09:47.699
dunked on all of them by hitting each of the
10.

00:09:47.699 --> 00:09:51.899
On July 23rd, the silver slugs that Beverly
was to fire at Pennywise were created, and

00:09:51.899 --> 00:09:55.949
two days later the seven of them turned up
to 29 Neibolt Street to confront It.

00:09:55.949 --> 00:09:59.120
Each of them perceive the house differently
based on their own fears, and for Mike, it

00:09:59.120 --> 00:10:02.439
gives him the same vibes he felt at the remains
of the Ironworks where he’d encountered

00:10:02.439 --> 00:10:03.439
the giant bird.

00:10:03.439 --> 00:10:06.140
The Losers venture upstairs and come across
three doors.

00:10:06.140 --> 00:10:09.730
The first contains a mattress that explodes
and oozes out black liquid, so they shut the

00:10:09.730 --> 00:10:11.140
door and move onto the second.

00:10:11.140 --> 00:10:14.370
When Beverly gets close to it she hears a
scream coming from the other side, and it

00:10:14.370 --> 00:10:17.300
has a buzzing quality making it sound like
a giant insect.

00:10:17.300 --> 00:10:21.300
Thanks to Mike’s farming expertise due to
many summers working for his father, he’s

00:10:21.300 --> 00:10:24.920
able to determine that this is not a monster,
but something known as a “moose blower”,

00:10:24.920 --> 00:10:29.220
a can that lets out a constant audible noise
in order to scare crows away from the crops.

00:10:29.220 --> 00:10:33.350
The last door contains a dilapidated bathroom
where Beverly is able to use the slingshot

00:10:33.350 --> 00:10:37.119
to drive It down into the sewers setting up
the final confrontation of the summer that

00:10:37.119 --> 00:10:39.110
would take place a couple weeks later.

00:10:39.110 --> 00:10:43.910
On August 10th, Mike is riding his bike through
town and notices a strange lack of activity

00:10:43.910 --> 00:10:46.370
and an ominous orange glow setting over the
sky.

00:10:46.370 --> 00:10:50.959
One of the only people he bumps into are his
friends, Bill is there with Stan, Richie and

00:10:50.959 --> 00:10:51.959
Eddie.

00:10:51.959 --> 00:10:55.139
They cross over to the Barrens side of Kansas
Street, where Ben and Beverly run up to them,

00:10:55.139 --> 00:10:58.459
going off about how Henry Bowers had come
after her for her life.

00:10:58.459 --> 00:11:02.119
Bill determines that Henry and his goons are
being driven by It, and decides it’s time

00:11:02.119 --> 00:11:03.779
to go after the monster once more.

00:11:03.779 --> 00:11:07.829
They go into The Barrens and rock flies out
of the bushes and strikes Mike in the head.

00:11:07.829 --> 00:11:10.519
It had come from Henry, with his goons Belch
and Victor.

00:11:10.519 --> 00:11:14.139
The move represents their revenge on Mike
for running to the others and luring the bullies

00:11:14.139 --> 00:11:17.420
into the rock fight where they were badly
bombarded with stones.

00:11:17.420 --> 00:11:21.220
Mike retaliates by throwing a piece of scrap
wood back at them before the Losers all escape

00:11:21.220 --> 00:11:22.220
to the sewers.

00:11:22.220 --> 00:11:26.360
The bullies came down into the sewers after
them, and Mike felt trapped between his two

00:11:26.360 --> 00:11:30.629
worst demons as he heard Henry’s screams
echoing off the pipes as he continued to pursue

00:11:30.629 --> 00:11:31.629
them.

00:11:31.629 --> 00:11:35.310
Luckily for him, Henry would not catch up
with for another 27 years, but what awaited

00:11:35.310 --> 00:11:38.800
Mike deeper under Derry was worse than he
could have ever imagined.

00:11:38.800 --> 00:11:42.310
First, he was restrained by the tentacles
of a giant crawling eye creature that threatened

00:11:42.310 --> 00:11:46.579
to crush him where he stood and left him powerless
to fight, it was only Eddie’s heroics that

00:11:46.579 --> 00:11:47.629
broke them free.

00:11:47.629 --> 00:11:51.220
The eye represented one of Richie’s fears,
but what would come was an incarnation of

00:11:51.220 --> 00:11:53.339
something Mike had long been afraid of.

00:11:53.339 --> 00:11:56.889
This is another detail that really cements
Mike’s position as the historian and also

00:11:56.889 --> 00:11:58.499
sets him apart from any of the others.

00:11:58.499 --> 00:12:02.160
When It takes the form of one of their fears,
it’s usually something recent that one of

00:12:02.160 --> 00:12:03.529
them saw and frightened them.

00:12:03.529 --> 00:12:07.019
For example, Richie sees a werewolf movie
and It becomes a werewolf shortly after to

00:12:07.019 --> 00:12:08.019
scare him.

00:12:08.019 --> 00:12:09.339
One possible exception is Stan.

00:12:09.339 --> 00:12:13.570
The Dead Boys he sees in his solo encounter
with It are from a news bite from many years

00:12:13.570 --> 00:12:17.829
ago, however, he only found out about it recently,
so it’s still more of a recent fear.

00:12:17.829 --> 00:12:22.089
But the other exception is Mike, whose fear
goes way back to a time he is hardly able

00:12:22.089 --> 00:12:24.889
to remember, the bird that attacked him in
his crib as a baby.

00:12:24.889 --> 00:12:29.439
The next form It takes is the giant bird,
a form that shows Mike’s eye for all things

00:12:29.440 --> 00:12:31.209
past AND present.

00:12:31.209 --> 00:12:35.000
The bird dives in and scratches Eddie, and
Mike retaliates by slashing his buck-knife

00:12:35.000 --> 00:12:35.999
into It’s talons.

00:12:35.999 --> 00:12:39.739
He tries to fight back with the knife again,
but misses and gets cut by the claws.

00:12:39.739 --> 00:12:43.139
Luckily, Stan is able to drive to creature
away with his knowledge of birds, likely saving

00:12:43.139 --> 00:12:47.610
the lives of Eddie and Mike if not all of
them, and allowing them to continue on into

00:12:47.610 --> 00:12:49.020
the lair of It.

00:12:55.020 --> 00:12:59.220
After supporting Bill in his interdimensional
mind battle with the monster, Mike and the

00:12:59.230 --> 00:13:03.850
others would escape the sewers and vow to
take care of It again if It had somehow survived.

00:13:03.850 --> 00:13:07.740
Mike involuntarily takes the position that
they would later refer to as “manning the

00:13:07.740 --> 00:13:10.970
lighthouse”, he stayed back in Derry to
keep an eye out for sign of It’s return

00:13:10.970 --> 00:13:12.769
over the next 27 years.

00:13:12.769 --> 00:13:16.750
Mike was stuck with this because his family
was the only one that did not move away, but

00:13:16.750 --> 00:13:19.579
it’s also fitting that he be the one to
stay for two reasons.

00:13:19.579 --> 00:13:23.449
First, the others lose their memories of the
events of the summer of 1958 when they leave,

00:13:23.449 --> 00:13:27.350
and Mike must retain his memories because
he is and always has been the book keeper,

00:13:27.350 --> 00:13:30.869
it’s his responsibility to fill them in
on the history of Derry and the history of

00:13:30.869 --> 00:13:33.209
their own quarrels with the monster when they
return.

00:13:33.209 --> 00:13:37.259
Second, by staying in Derry, Mike is able
to continue to research Derry’s dark past

00:13:37.259 --> 00:13:41.959
and dig out the details necessary to combat
It, should another confrontation be necessary.

00:13:41.959 --> 00:13:45.489
Before that happens though, Mike must face
some of the toughest years of his life.

00:13:45.489 --> 00:13:50.189
In 1962, when Mike was 15 years old, his father
was hospitalized with cancer.

00:13:50.189 --> 00:13:53.869
He would go to visit his dad every day on
his bike, because even four years after the

00:13:53.869 --> 00:13:57.360
murders in Derry had ceased, his mother was
still uncomfortable with his trying to hitch

00:13:57.360 --> 00:13:58.360
a ride.

00:13:58.360 --> 00:14:01.320
During one of these visits, Will told his
son one last story that he had yet to pass

00:14:01.320 --> 00:14:03.910
on, the story of the Black Spot fire.

00:14:03.910 --> 00:14:07.320
In 1930, during Will’s time in the army,
he helped open up a nightclub that he and

00:14:07.329 --> 00:14:08.579
his friends would be welcome at.

00:14:08.579 --> 00:14:12.470
The jazz joint became pretty popular, and
white troops started showing up there as well,

00:14:12.470 --> 00:14:15.800
until one night an evil organisation set fire
to the place.

00:14:15.800 --> 00:14:20.050
After narrowly escaping, Will looked up and
saw the giant bird, not flapping its wings,

00:14:20.050 --> 00:14:22.619
but floating with a red balloon tied to each
side.

00:14:22.619 --> 00:14:26.899
This event suggests that It has some kind
of generational hold on both Hanlons and gives

00:14:26.899 --> 00:14:32.029
Mike the confirmation that the seemingly random
acts of malice may all go back to the monster.

00:14:32.029 --> 00:14:35.839
Still, he couldn’t have known if It would
reawaken again, or if he and his friends had

00:14:35.839 --> 00:14:39.410
actually killed it in ‘58, so he continued
to keep an eye out.

00:14:39.410 --> 00:14:43.029
His father would end up passing away that
year, but he and his Mom would stay in Derry,

00:14:43.029 --> 00:14:46.589
and Mike would continue his education at Derry
High School, where he became the running back

00:14:46.589 --> 00:14:47.649
of the football team.

00:14:47.649 --> 00:14:51.420
The former Losers Club member didn’t achieve
the levels of success his friends did when

00:14:51.420 --> 00:14:54.939
they grew up -- something Mike attributes
to their triumph over It leading to success

00:14:54.939 --> 00:14:58.929
in other endeavors -- but I think it’s interesting
to note that Mike was able to graduate from

00:14:58.929 --> 00:15:02.949
marching band trombonist, to actually being
on the field during the football games.

00:15:02.949 --> 00:15:05.949
All of them kind of moved up in the world
after defeating It.

00:15:05.949 --> 00:15:10.059
At some point, Mike became the town librarian
and started to conduct deeper research about

00:15:10.059 --> 00:15:11.350
the past of Derry.

00:15:11.350 --> 00:15:15.199
In 1979, he must have realized that he’d
soon find out if It would be reawakening,

00:15:15.199 --> 00:15:19.130
because he subscribed to newspapers in the
six cities his old friends now lived in in

00:15:19.130 --> 00:15:20.209
order to keep tabs.

00:15:20.209 --> 00:15:24.399
It was around 1980 that he started to sense
that It would in fact come back.

00:15:24.399 --> 00:15:27.179
He claims the voice of The Turtle may have
clued him in on this.

00:15:27.179 --> 00:15:32.249
Also in 1980, he begins work on a book: Derry,
An Unauthorized Town History by Michael Hanlon.

00:15:32.249 --> 00:15:36.230
He starts his research by talking to a former
Derry librarian, a man by the name of Albert

00:15:36.230 --> 00:15:37.230
Carson.

00:15:37.230 --> 00:15:41.029
Carson discourages him from digging into Derry’s
past, suggesting that the facts that aren’t

00:15:41.029 --> 00:15:45.089
recorded in Derry’s history books may disturb
him, but Mike continues to press, so Carson

00:15:45.089 --> 00:15:46.080
gives him a couple of leads.

00:15:46.080 --> 00:15:47.120
the man who poisoned

00:15:47.120 --> 00:15:52.060
his family in 1851, the hacked up lumberjacks
of 1879, and more gruesome details of the

00:15:52.061 --> 00:15:54.379
Ironworks explosion that he already knew about.

00:15:54.379 --> 00:15:58.549
He also learns there was a man named Branson
Buddinger who tried to write a piece similar

00:15:58.549 --> 00:16:02.050
to what Mike is doing, but is essentially
driven mad and died.

00:16:02.050 --> 00:16:05.959
Despite this, Mike finds the bravery to continue
researching Derry, and becomes an important

00:16:05.959 --> 00:16:07.970
member of the community over the years.

00:16:07.970 --> 00:16:11.619
At some point in the 80s, the Aladdin Theater,
where he and the Losers used to spend part

00:16:11.619 --> 00:16:15.970
of their summers, is in danger of being shut
down, and Mike helped to call a town meeting

00:16:15.970 --> 00:16:16.970
to save it.

00:16:16.970 --> 00:16:20.149
Despite the noble act of saving a movie theater,
I think getting involved in the business of

00:16:20.149 --> 00:16:24.139
Derry was actually a mistake, but I’ll come
back to why I think that in a little bit.

00:16:24.139 --> 00:16:27.910
Mike took note when the murders started up
again in the year 1984, but didn’t want

00:16:27.910 --> 00:16:31.819
to call the other Losers back to Derry until
he was absolutely sure that It was back.

00:16:31.819 --> 00:16:36.019
He got really close to calling them in February
of 1985 when the disappearances of Dennis

00:16:36.019 --> 00:16:38.560
Torio and Lori Anne Winterbarger took place.

00:16:38.560 --> 00:16:42.179
Mike started paying off one of the Derry police
officers for more information and copies of

00:16:42.180 --> 00:16:45.100
evidence photos for his own documentation.

00:16:45.100 --> 00:16:48.500
"Chief's gonna have a cow when he sees you nosing around Mike."

00:16:48.500 --> 00:16:49.740
"I won't tell him if you don't."

00:16:49.900 --> 00:16:53.310
In March, he stays late at the library one
night and finds a balloon tied to his reading

00:16:53.310 --> 00:16:55.609
lamp with a photo of him attached.

00:16:55.609 --> 00:16:59.339
One drunken night in April, Mike reads about
Claude Heroux and the crimes he committed

00:16:59.339 --> 00:17:00.720
in 1905.

00:17:00.720 --> 00:17:04.449
That night, he also gets the sense that It
wants revenge for when the Losers nearly killed

00:17:04.449 --> 00:17:05.510
it as kids.

00:17:05.510 --> 00:17:09.929
Mike keeps on documenting the incidents that
take place through May 22, when a 5th grader

00:17:09.929 --> 00:17:14.709
named Jerry Bellwood is found alongside the
words Come Home printed on a cement wall in

00:17:14.709 --> 00:17:15.709
blood.

00:17:15.709 --> 00:17:19.929
That ends up being the final straw before
Mike calls his six childhood friends back

00:17:19.929 --> 00:17:20.929
to Derry.

00:17:20.929 --> 00:17:24.529
He sets up a reunion lunch near the recently
built mall at a Chinese place called Jade

00:17:24.529 --> 00:17:25.529
of the Orient.

00:17:25.529 --> 00:17:29.179
His reasoning for choosing it, is that it’s
new, and he probably know better than anyone

00:17:29.179 --> 00:17:32.380
that It has a stranglehold on everything from
Derry’s past.

00:17:32.380 --> 00:17:36.380
Only five of them make it to the reunion,
and Mike has to explain how Stan had passed

00:17:36.380 --> 00:17:37.380
away.

00:17:37.380 --> 00:17:40.470
He fills them in on everything, I just said
in the last 4-5 minutes of this video that

00:17:40.470 --> 00:17:41.840
I don’t care to repeat.

00:17:41.840 --> 00:17:46.100
As the Losers spend more time back in Derry,
their childhood scars start to come back,

00:17:46.100 --> 00:17:50.330
and Mike reveals claw scars on his chest,
he would have acquired against the giant bird

00:17:50.330 --> 00:17:52.370
in the sewers 27 years ago.

00:17:52.370 --> 00:17:55.630
Things start to get weird when they all get
their fortune cookies, but they try to play

00:17:55.630 --> 00:17:58.480
it cool when the waitress comes by as not
to raise alarm.

00:17:58.480 --> 00:18:00.669
“So who do you think’s going to win the
pennant?”

00:18:00.669 --> 00:18:02.760
Bill asked Mike, smiling insanely.

00:18:02.760 --> 00:18:05.410
Rose came through the curtain just then, her
face politely questioning.

00:18:05.410 --> 00:18:08.669
“I think the Chicago Bears look good,”
Mike said.

00:18:08.669 --> 00:18:12.450
If only he had seen them on Monday Night Football
this week against Washington!

00:18:12.450 --> 00:18:13.480
Khalil Mack!

00:18:13.480 --> 00:18:14.669
Danny Travathan!

00:18:14.669 --> 00:18:16.110
Ha-Ha Clinton Pick Six!

00:18:16.110 --> 00:18:20.210
No, but the book takes place in 1985, which
of course is the year that The Bears won the

00:18:20.210 --> 00:18:21.210
Super Bowl.

00:18:21.210 --> 00:18:25.420
The movie, It Chapter 2, takes place in 2016,
so it would have been an excellent opportunity

00:18:25.420 --> 00:18:27.260
to do that same scene but with a different
answer.

00:18:27.270 --> 00:18:28.900
“So who do you think’s going to win the
pennant?”

00:18:28.910 --> 00:18:31.159
“I think the Chicago Cubs look good.”

00:18:31.159 --> 00:18:33.549
Anyway, where even was I?

00:18:33.549 --> 00:18:34.549
Right.

00:18:34.549 --> 00:18:35.549
Mike Hanlon.

00:18:35.549 --> 00:18:38.360
They all go their separate ways and plan to
meet at the library later, and during this

00:18:38.360 --> 00:18:41.809
down time, Mike gets a call from Bill, asking
if he can store a bike he just bought in Mike’s

00:18:41.809 --> 00:18:46.000
shed, and Mike somehow knows right away that
it’s Bill’s old bike, Silver, and says

00:18:46.000 --> 00:18:47.000
yes.

00:18:47.000 --> 00:18:50.620
They fix up the bike together with a patch
kit Mike bought a week beforehand on an impulse,

00:18:50.620 --> 00:18:52.490
even though he doesn’t even own a bike.

00:18:52.490 --> 00:18:56.240
This is more evidence that there was a “helping
hand” at play this time, just as the Turtle

00:18:56.240 --> 00:19:00.480
helped them in 1958, there was a different
hand of fate guiding them as adults.

00:19:00.480 --> 00:19:04.440
Now when Mike joined the group after the rock
fight 27 years ago, he felt himself become

00:19:04.440 --> 00:19:05.500
the final piece.

00:19:05.500 --> 00:19:08.880
The wheel was complete, and it could begin
to roll, and that’s when they started making

00:19:08.880 --> 00:19:10.190
plans to fight Pennywise.

00:19:10.190 --> 00:19:13.770
The reason Mike had them all walk around town
and regain their memories was to see if they

00:19:13.770 --> 00:19:17.320
could close that wheel again, it would be
smaller without Stan, but it was the only

00:19:17.320 --> 00:19:22.340
chance they had to defeat It, but that evening
Mike’s plan would go horribly wrong.

00:19:28.960 --> 00:19:34.200
It was 1:15AM after another meeting with the
Losers at the Derry Public Library when Mike

00:19:34.210 --> 00:19:37.080
advised them all to go back to the hotel and
get some sleep.

00:19:37.080 --> 00:19:40.700
He decided to stay a bit longer and log the
night’s events in his journal, but he had

00:19:40.700 --> 00:19:43.380
a strange feeling he wasn’t alone in the
library.

00:19:43.380 --> 00:19:47.220
Fifteen minutes later he hears a footstep,
and approaches with a letter opener as his

00:19:47.220 --> 00:19:48.320
only defense.

00:19:48.320 --> 00:19:52.310
It was his old enemy, Henry Bowers, freed
from the mental asylum he’d been locked

00:19:52.310 --> 00:19:53.520
up in by It.

00:19:53.520 --> 00:19:56.559
Henry has his old blade back as well, and
the two go at it.

00:19:56.559 --> 00:20:00.470
It eggs Henry on by taking the form of Stan’s
head and then later Belch’s head on the

00:20:00.470 --> 00:20:03.440
library circulation desk and telling him to
finish Mike off.

00:20:03.440 --> 00:20:07.309
Ultimately, Mike’s letter opener is enough
to fend him off though, and Henry flees the

00:20:07.309 --> 00:20:11.240
library thinking that Mike had lost enough
blood to do him in, but pretty badly injured

00:20:11.240 --> 00:20:12.240
himself.

00:20:12.240 --> 00:20:15.090
Mike is barely able to make it to the phone
to call 911.

00:20:15.090 --> 00:20:18.990
Pennywise messes with him in the process,
by taking over the telephone line Mike is

00:20:18.990 --> 00:20:23.080
trying to talk on and replacing the clock
face with the face of Will Hanlon.

00:20:23.080 --> 00:20:27.059
Police find Mike barely hanging on when they
arrive and transfer him to the hospital, where

00:20:27.059 --> 00:20:29.230
It would make one more attempt on his life.

00:20:29.230 --> 00:20:32.580
The other five decided that the longer they
waited to take on It, the more danger they

00:20:32.580 --> 00:20:33.799
were putting themselves in.

00:20:33.799 --> 00:20:37.789
For a long time, it seemed strange to me that
the novel is told from Mike’s perspective

00:20:37.789 --> 00:20:41.269
more than anyone else's, but he isn’t there
for the final confrontation, but on further

00:20:41.269 --> 00:20:44.240
examination, I think that’s exactly the
reason that he couldn’t be there for the

00:20:44.240 --> 00:20:45.240
final fight.

00:20:45.240 --> 00:20:48.659
Remember earlier, when I mentioned Mike getting
involved in the community to save the theater?

00:20:48.659 --> 00:20:51.260
I think he basically acclimated himself into
Derry.

00:20:51.260 --> 00:20:55.750
He stayed there and became a part of the town,
and as we know, Pennywise rules all things

00:20:55.750 --> 00:20:56.750
Derry.

00:20:56.750 --> 00:20:59.850
He may have had good intentions, but he was
really no more capable of stopping It than

00:20:59.850 --> 00:21:02.660
characters like Mr. Nell and Mr. Gedreau.

00:21:02.660 --> 00:21:06.540
Mike stays the night in the hospital and over
the next four hours, a huge storm brews above

00:21:06.540 --> 00:21:09.809
Derry as his friends make their way towards
the lair of It.

00:21:09.809 --> 00:21:12.409
At 6:46AM, Mike awakens with a bad feeling.

00:21:12.409 --> 00:21:16.910
It has possessed one of the nurses at the
hospital, Marc Lemonica, the brother of one

00:21:16.910 --> 00:21:19.440
of the victims, who was taken by It in 1958.

00:21:19.440 --> 00:21:22.830
He’s planning on overdosing Mike with a
loaded syringe, and Mike doesn’t have the

00:21:22.830 --> 00:21:24.500
physical strength to stop him.

00:21:24.500 --> 00:21:27.340
At that moment, Bill and the others sense
Mike is in danger.

00:21:27.340 --> 00:21:30.971
They join hands and telekinetically send some
of their power to him, and instance of the

00:21:30.971 --> 00:21:35.110
Losers Club using The Shine to aid their friend,
but for some reason when the Losers sense

00:21:35.110 --> 00:21:38.720
Mike is in danger it always reminds me more
of the destruction of Alderaan in Star Wars.

00:21:40.220 --> 00:21:41.220
“Are you alright?

00:21:41.320 --> 00:21:42.300
What’s wrong?”

00:21:43.840 --> 00:21:45.860
“I felt a great disturbance in the Force.

00:21:45.870 --> 00:21:49.220
As if millions of voices suddenly cried out
in terror.

00:21:49.220 --> 00:21:51.330
And were suddenly silenced.”

00:21:51.330 --> 00:21:54.759
Maybe we could draw some comparisons to the
abilities held by the characters in King’s

00:21:54.759 --> 00:21:58.509
writing and “the Force”, but that sounds
like a fan-fiction for another day.

00:21:58.509 --> 00:22:01.870
The power from his friends gives Mike the
ability to pick up a bottle and crack it over

00:22:01.870 --> 00:22:02.970
Lamonica’s head.

00:22:02.970 --> 00:22:06.220
Bill and Richie had the strength to continue
on and defeat Pennywise knowing their friend

00:22:06.220 --> 00:22:07.590
Mike would be OK.

00:22:07.590 --> 00:22:09.170
Mike ended up spending the week in the hospital.

00:22:09.170 --> 00:22:12.880
On June 4th, Bill dropped by to bring him
his manuscript and he offered up his place

00:22:12.880 --> 00:22:16.450
to Bill and his wife, who was trying to recover
from her encounter with It’s deadlights.

00:22:16.450 --> 00:22:20.750
They are all starting to lose their memories
again, but this time, Mike is losing his as

00:22:20.750 --> 00:22:24.549
well, because with Pennywise dead, there is
no reason he needs to hold onto that trauma

00:22:24.549 --> 00:22:25.549
any longer.

00:22:25.549 --> 00:22:29.539
He also feels that with It gone, Derry is
dying as well, which ties in nicely to my

00:22:29.539 --> 00:22:32.980
theory about Mike not joining in on the final
battle because he had become an integral part

00:22:32.980 --> 00:22:33.980
of Derry.

00:22:33.980 --> 00:22:37.700
By June 11th, the day Mike was discharged
from the hospital, he had nearly completely

00:22:37.700 --> 00:22:40.850
forgotten everything about his group of friends
from 1958.

00:22:40.850 --> 00:22:45.299
He tried writing everything down, the only
logical approach he could take being the group’s

00:22:45.299 --> 00:22:49.370
record keeper, but the words faded from the
pages hours after he wrote them.

00:22:49.370 --> 00:22:53.340
Mike has grown tired of Derry and likely moves
on from It after the end of the novel, with

00:22:53.340 --> 00:22:55.080
him no longer needing to keep watch.

00:22:55.080 --> 00:22:59.919
But before he leaves, he makes one final dedication
to the town he spent so much of his life in.

00:22:59.919 --> 00:23:04.170
He commissions a memorial plaque at the site
the standpipe once stood before it was swept

00:23:04.170 --> 00:23:05.880
away in the terrible storm.

00:23:05.880 --> 00:23:07.030
TO THOSE LOST IN THE STORM.

00:23:07.030 --> 00:23:08.030
MAY 31, 1985.

00:23:08.030 --> 00:23:09.100
And to the children.

00:23:09.100 --> 00:23:10.190
All the children.

00:23:10.190 --> 00:23:15.149
Love Bill, Ben, Bev, Eddie, Richie, Stan,
Mike.

00:23:15.149 --> 00:23:16.389
The Losers Club.

00:23:16.389 --> 00:23:20.830
Even after moving onto a new life and finally
forgetting about the best friends of his childhood,

00:23:20.830 --> 00:23:23.179
he would sometimes still encounter them in
his dreams.

00:23:23.179 --> 00:23:27.029
If you want to hear my analysis of the
other members of the Losers Club click that

00:23:27.029 --> 00:23:28.300
playlist on the left.

00:23:28.300 --> 00:23:31.490
And there are a couple more coming soon so
if you don’t want to miss out on those make

00:23:31.490 --> 00:23:36.710
sure you subscribe to CZsWorld for new horrors
every week, ring that deathbell for notifications

00:23:36.710 --> 00:23:38.679
and I’ll see you in the next one.

00:23:38.679 --> 00:23:41.139
Assuming we both survive.

